Dictionaries-

syntax- Dic={
"name":"Akash",
"age":20,
"address":"Kanpur"
}
print(Dic.keys()) out- name, age, address
print(Dic.values())  out- Akash, 20, Kanpur 

print(Dic.get("full name")) output- None  because there is no key full name in dictionary
print(Dic.get("full name","Not Found")) output- Not Found  because there is no key full name in dictionary but we give default value Not Found so it will print Not Found

Dic["full name"]="Akash Kumar"  add this is how we can add new key value pair in dictionary

Dic["name"]="Rahul"  this is how we can update the value of existing key in dictionary







                      
              
